Windgrace's Judgment: "For any number of opponents, destroy target
nonland permanent that player controls."

phase split off "For any number of opponents" as an unrecognized clause
head and parsed the rest as a destroy of a permanent its controller
controls, so the spell could not be cast at all.

CR 115.1 + CR 601.2c: choosing any number of opponents and, for each,
one target that opponent controls is choosing any number of targets that
opponents control, no two controlled by the same player. The effect
chain now parses the instruction in that equivalent wording ("destroy
any number of target nonland permanent an opponent controls controlled
by different players"), which the existing grammar lowers to an
unbounded multi-target (minimum 0) with
TargetSelectionConstraint::DifferentObjectControllers.

Card data: reaches games only with card data generated by this parser.

Test: tests/integration/windgraces_judgment_one_per_opponent.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
